The Atlas engine is fetched at build time from Enntity/atlas at the commit in
install/atlas-source.json (AGPL-3.0-only): Atlas-Inf plus SparkGLM's GLM-5.3
Flash work, which started as Reiner Schmidt's port in Mango-kid/atlas
(AGPL-3.0-only).

The overlay converter's NVFP4 quantization kernel is copied unchanged from
Atlas-Inf/atlas, by way of Mango-kid/atlas (AGPL-3.0-only); see
install/converter/provenance.json.

FlashKDA by MoonshotAI (MIT, LICENSES/MIT-FlashKDA.txt) is fetched and patched
at build time; install/flash_kda/flash_kda_sm121_slots.patch carries both MIT
and AGPL terms, and install/flash_kda/atlas_flash_kda_bridge.cu adapts
FlashKDA's workspace-size and launch arithmetic.

FlashInfer (Apache-2.0, LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt) and CUTLASS (BSD-3-Clause)
are fetched at build time. NVIDIA's sparse-MLA SM120 prefill source inside
FlashInfer is BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES
(LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause-NVIDIA.txt). The image ships these notices under
/opt/atlas/notices/.

install/start-node.sh and install/convert.sh follow LLooM's Atlas recipe
(MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 LLooM contributors, LICENSES/MIT-LLooM.txt).

SparkGLM grew out of MiaAI-Lab's GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks recipe (MIT,
Copyright (c) 2026 Mia's AI Lab, LICENSES/MIT-Mia.txt). .github/FUNDING.yml
and the mia-* prompts in bench/staggered_openai.py come from it. The vLLM-era
tree, with its complete notices and attributions, is preserved at the tag
vllm-final.

The bench/mmastrac_*.py prompts are quoted from mmastrac/glm-5.3-flash-4x-gx10
for comparability.

Model weights are not distributed in this repository. They remain under their
publishers' licenses; the DFlash2 drafter is CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 (non-commercial).
See docs/LICENSING.md.
